    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch01-item-2-1",
      "sourceStart": 1523,
      "sourceEnd": 1637,
      "original": "### 2.1. A subset $U\\subseteq V$ is a subspace of $V$ if and only if $U$ satisfies the following three conditions:",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch01-block-0008",
      "sourceStart": 1637,
      "sourceEnd": 1743,
      "sha256": "e2d6c1528387ed0375b30df55c905d4dad76f87cb2cc7fbca93b049db329b6c7"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch01-item-2-2",
      "sourceStart": 1743,
      "sourceEnd": 1878,
      "original": "### 2.2. For subspaces $V_1,\\ldots,V_n$ of a vector space, their sum, defined below, is the smallest subspace that contains each $V_k$.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch01-block-0009",
      "sourceStart": 1878,
      "sourceEnd": 1971,
      "sha256": "90f9ade2c409b71b2dda56fd80a7df0a262b3ddb6d87136b46ef244cfe2ba565"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch01-item-2-3",
      "sourceStart": 1971,
      "sourceEnd": 2152,
      "original": "### 2.3. Let $V_1,\\ldots,V_m$ be subspaces of $V$. Then $V_1+\\ldots+V_m$ is a direct sum if and only if the only way to write $0$ as a sum $v_1+\\ldots+v_m$ is by taking all $v_k=0$.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch01-block-0010",
      "sourceStart": 2152,
      "sourceEnd": 2154,
      "sha256": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch01-item-2-4",
      "sourceStart": 2154,
      "sourceEnd": 2203,
      "original": "### 2.4. Suppose $U,W$ are subspaces of $V$. Then",
